{"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/Trie","type":"reference"},{"text":" is a set of sequences and a ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/TrieDictionary","type":"reference"},{"text":" a dictionary keyed by them, both kept in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a trie (Fredkin, 1960): a tree whose edges carry symbols and whose root-to-vertex paths spell the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"keys. They answer the queries a hash set cannot: every key with a prefix","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(","type":"text"},{"code":"elements(withPrefix:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", whose ","type":"text"},{"code":"count","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is O(1)), whether any key has one (","type":"text"},{"code":"hasPrefix(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"), and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the longest key that is a prefix of a query (","type":"text"},{"code":"longestPrefix(of:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":").","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["import Tries","","let words = Trie([\"car\", \"cart\", \"cat\", \"dog\"])","words.contains(\"cat\")                                   \/\/ true","words.elements(withPrefix: \"car\").map { String($0) }    \/\/ [\"car\", \"cart\"]","words.longestPrefix(of: \"carton\").map { String($0) }    \/\/ \"cart\""]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Keys are any sequence of the symbol type and are stored as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"[Symbol]"},{"type":"text","text":". For text, the symbol"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"type decides what a step is: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Trie<Character>"},{"type":"text","text":" steps by grapheme cluster, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Trie<Unicode.Scalar>"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"by scalar, and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Trie<UInt8>"},{"type":"text","text":" over "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"utf8"},{"type":"text","text":" by byte, the fastest of the three, because comparing"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"bytes is cheaper than comparing "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Character"},{"type":"text","text":"s. When the symbols are "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Comparable"},{"type":"text","text":", each vertex keeps"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"its children sorted, so iteration is in lexicographic order; otherwise children come in the order"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"they were added."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/RadixTree","type":"reference"},{"text":" and a ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/RadixTreeDictionary","type":"reference"},{"text":" hold the same keys and answer the same queries,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"with the same names, in a radix tree (Morrison, 1968): every chain of vertices with one child and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"no key is merged into one edge labelled with all its symbols, so there is a vertex per key and per","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"branching point rather than per symbol. They suit keys with long shared prefixes, such as file","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"paths or URLs, and build faster and in less memory than a trie of the same keys.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A trie’s shape converts to Grafluent’s "},{"code":"PrefixTree","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" with "},{"code":"PrefixTree(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and a radix tree’s to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"an "},{"code":"Arborescence","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" of its vertices’ prefixes with "},{"code":"Arborescence(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" (import Grafluent’s "},{"code":"Trees","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"module beside this one)."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/AhoCorasickAutomaton","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" (Aho and Corasick, 1975) finds every occurrence of any of a set of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"patterns in one pass over a text, in O("},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"n"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" + "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"z","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":") for "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"n","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" symbols and "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"z","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" matches: a trie of the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"patterns with failure links. Its "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/AhoCorasickAutomaton\/statesView-swift.property","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" is the automaton as a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DirectedGraph"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let automaton = AhoCorasickAutomaton(patterns: [\"he\", \"she\", \"his\", \"hers\"])","automaton.matches(in: \"ushers\").map(\\.patternIndex)   \/\/ [1, 0, 3]"]}],"kind":"content"}],"sections":[],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/tries"]}],"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/Trie","doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/RadixTree"],"anchor":"Sets-of-sequences","title":"Sets of sequences"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/TrieDictionary","doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/RadixTreeDictionary"],"anchor":"Dictionaries-keyed-by-sequences","title":"Dictionaries keyed by sequences"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/AhoCorasickAutomaton"],"anchor":"Pattern-matching","title":"Pattern matching"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/Trees"],"anchor":"Extended-Modules","title":"Extended Modules","generated":true}],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"Tries"}],"role":"collection","symbolKind":"module","externalID":"Tries","title":"Tries","roleHeading":"Framework"},"kind":"symbol","identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"abstract":[{"text":"Tries over sequences of any ","type":"text"},{"code":"Hashable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" symbols, with prefix queries, and multi-pattern matching.","type":"text"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"references":{"doc://Tries/documentation/Tries":{"role":"collection","title":"Tries","identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/tries","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Tries over sequences of any "},{"code":"Hashable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" symbols, with prefix queries, and multi-pattern matching."}]},"doc://Tries/documentation/Tries/AhoCorasickAutomaton":{"role":"symbol","title":"AhoCorasickAutomaton","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"AhoCorasickAutomaton","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/AhoCorasickAutomaton","url":"\/documentation\/tries\/ahocorasickautomaton","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An automaton that finds every occurrence of every pattern of a set in one pass over a text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(Aho and Corasick, 1975)."}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"AhoCorasickAutomaton","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://Tries/documentation/Tries/RadixTree":{"role":"symbol","title":"RadixTree","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"RadixTree","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/RadixTree","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/tries\/radixtree","abstract":[{"text":"A set of sequences kept in a radix tree (Morrison, 1968): a trie in which every chain of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vertices with one child and no key is merged into one edge labelled with all its symbols.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"RadixTree","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://Tries/documentation/Tries/TrieDictionary":{"abstract":[{"text":"A dictionary keyed by sequences, kept in a trie: a tree whose edges carry symbols and whose","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"root-to-vertex paths spell the keys, each key’s vertex holding its value (Fredkin, 1960).","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/tries\/triedictionary","title":"TrieDictionary","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"TrieDictionary"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"TrieDictionary"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/TrieDictionary"},"doc://Tries/documentation/Tries/AhoCorasickAutomaton/StatesView-swift.struct/symbol(ofEdgeAt:)":{"role":"symbol","title":"symbol(ofEdgeAt:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/AhoCorasickAutomaton\/StatesView-swift.struct\/symbol(ofEdgeAt:)","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/tries\/ahocorasickautomaton\/statesview-swift.struct\/symbol(ofedgeat:)","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"The symbol a goto edge reads, or nil for a failure edge.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"symbol","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"ofEdgeAt","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","text":"Int","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Symbol","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}]},"doc://Tries/documentation/Tries/RadixTreeDictionary":{"type":"topic","title":"RadixTreeDictionary","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/RadixTreeDictionary","url":"\/documentation\/tries\/radixtreedictionary","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A dictionary keyed by sequences, kept in a radix tree (Morrison, 1968): a trie in which every"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"chain of vertices with one child and no key is merged into one edge labelled with all its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"symbols, each key’s vertex holding its value."}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"RadixTreeDictionary","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"RadixTreeDictionary","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://Tries/documentation/Tries/AhoCorasickAutomaton/statesView-swift.property":{"title":"statesView","type":"topic","conformance":{"availabilityPrefix":[{"text":"Available when","type":"text"}],"conformancePrefix":[{"text":"Conforms when","type":"text"}],"constraints":[{"code":"Symbol","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" conforms to ","type":"text"},{"code":"Hashable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/AhoCorasickAutomaton\/statesView-swift.property","url":"\/documentation\/tries\/ahocorasickautomaton\/statesview-swift.property","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The automaton’s states as a directed graph: a vertex per state, numbered from 0 for the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"root, a goto edge from each state to each of its trie children, and a failure edge from"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"each state but the root to its failure state. "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/AhoCorasickAutomaton\/StatesView-swift.struct\/symbol(ofEdgeAt:)"},{"type":"text","text":" tells the two"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"apart."}],"fragments":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"statesView","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"AhoCorasickAutomaton","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:5Tries20AhoCorasickAutomatonV"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Symbol","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">.","kind":"text"},{"text":"StatesView","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:5Tries20AhoCorasickAutomatonV10StatesViewV"}]},"doc://Tries/documentation/Tries/Trees":{"role":"collection","title":"Trees","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/Trees","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/tries\/trees","abstract":[]},"doc://Tries/documentation/Tries/Trie":{"abstract":[{"text":"A set of sequences kept in a trie: a tree whose edges carry symbols and whose root-to-vertex","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"paths spell the keys (Fredkin, 1960).","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/tries\/trie","title":"Trie","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Trie"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Trie"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/Trie"}}}